    "created_at": "2017-05-22T13:56:07Z",
    "updated_at": "2017-05-22T13:56:07Z",
    "body": "Is this consistent with ECMAScript?  I'm not an expert, but neither of [7.3.21EnumerableOwnProperties](https://tc39.github.io/ecma262/#sec-enumerableownproperties) nor [13.7.5.15EnumerateObjectProperties](https://tc39.github.io/ecma262/#sec-enumerate-object-properties) seem throwing an exception.  Probably I should look at different places.  I'm just wondering if it's consistent with ECMAScript or not, and if not, we can update the spec instead of the implementations.\r\n",
    "author_association": "NONE",
    "pin": null,
    "reactions": {
      "url": "https://api.github.com/repos/whatwg/webidl/issues/comments/303107230/reactions",
